  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Given that $\u2016v\u2016=6$ and $u\\cdot v=-9$, find the smallest possible value of $\u2016u\u2016.$",
  "worked_solution": "Using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, we have   \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|u\\cdot v| & \\le \u2016u\u2016\\cdot \u2016v\u2016 \\\\ |-9| & \\le \u2016u\u2016\\cdot 6 \\\\ 9 & \\le 6\\cdot \u2016u\u2016 \\\\ 3 & \\le 2\\cdot \u2016u\u2016.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply both sides of the inequality by $\\frac{1}{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3 & \\le \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot \u2016u\u2016 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} & \\le \u2016u\u2016\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $\u2016u\u2016$\nis  $\\frac{3}{2}.$",
